&lt;h3&gt;


  The Anti-Optimization List (Don't Do These)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Anti-Pattern&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Why&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt; on every computation&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Overhead of memoization &amp;gt; savings on cheap ops&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;React.memo&lt;/code&gt; on everything&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Comparison cost on frequently-changing props is wasteful&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Premature code splitting&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;50 tiny chunks cause more network overhead than one medium bundle&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Over-abstracting for "performance"&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Added complexity makes code harder to maintain and debug&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Optimizing without measuring&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;You might optimize the wrong thing entirely&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Remember: &lt;strong&gt;measure first, then optimize the bottleneck, then measure again&lt;/strong&gt;. Performance optimization is a science, not a guessing game.&lt;/p&gt;




